News - What are the functions and precautions of the laboratory centrifuge tubes?
In many laboratories, there is a glass or plastic vessel composed of a hemispherical bottom and a cylinder, which is used to place radioactive or highly corrosive samples. It is a centrifuge tube.
It is suitable for some chemicals. Precautions for the centrifuge tubes: When we use the centrifuge tube, do not use one tube multiple times, pay attention to the volatilization of the sample and the leakage of some radioactive or corrosive samples; in the storage process, it must be sealed; Prevent the centrifuge tube from being deformed during use.
The precautions for the use of centrifuge tubes, have you done it right?
The centrifuge tube should be heated evenly when heated, otherwise it will bump or the test tube will burst; the centrifuge tube cannot be quenched after heating, otherwise it may break.
When the centrifuge tube is heated, keep the outer wall of the test tube free of water droplets to prevent uneven heating and bursting.
The centrifuge tube contains very few objects, a small amount of gas, liquid or solid, and a small amount is also standard. Generally, it does not exceed 1/2 of the capacity of the test tube when it is filled with a solution, and it does not exceed 1/3 of the test tube when it is heated.
When heating the centrifuge tube containing solids, the nozzle of the tube should be slightly downward, and the liquid should be tilted about 45 ° when heating the liquid.
