In terms of the three most commonly used principles in the market, the detection rate of acoustic magnetic systems is the highest, generally exceeding 95%; radio / RF systems is between 60-80%, and electromagnetic waves are generally between 50 and 70%. The system with low detection rate is likely to have the leakage rate when the commodity is brought out, so the detection rate is one of the main performance indicators to evaluate the quality of the anti-theft system.
If a non-labeled item triggers the alarm, it will bring difficulties to the staff to judge and handle it, and even cause conflicts between customers and the mall. Due to the principle limitation, the current common EAS systems cannot completely exclude the false alarm, but there will be differences in performance, the key to choosing the system is to see the false alarm rate.
When the equipment is disturbed (primarily by the power supply and the surrounding noise), the system sends an alarm signal when no one passes or no triggered alarm item passes, a phenomenon called false report or self-alarm.
