First of all, I would like to welcome you to Siem Reap, a city of peace and full of historical and cultural heritages.
Looking into our past and present regional security cooperation, we have advanced gradually particularly in confidence and trust building and institutional enhancement.
We have witnessed the gradual development of the culture of frank and open dialogues in order to preserve peace and stability in the region. Social capital – that includes trust, confidence, and friendship – in the security sector has been improved remarkably and this has set a strong foundation for the regional security connectivity.
This is no longer a “zero-sum game” environment, and the entire region has worked very well to reduce the security dilemma that used to be rampant in our region. In short, our ASEAN region has moved from the “competitive security” mindset towards the norm of “cooperative security”.
I believe that large part of all the above progresses have been achieved due to our continued dialogues and discussion to solve common problems. The ADMM and ADMM-Plus are no doubt among the most important security architectures in this process.
Along this line , Cambodia has considered and submitted a new initiative for regional consideration due to positive development in each country in the region. That is, the possibility of making our ASEAN region to become a Civil war Free Zone.
We believe that through such active engagement and dialogue between ASEAN and the Plus countries, we can further strengthen mutual understanding and more effectively and efficiently address the common emerging regional security issues.
In closing, I would like to wish you all good health and great success in our common endeavor! And I hope you have time to visit our great country which is blessed by total peace brought about by the Win-Win Policy of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of the Kingdom of Cambodia.
