( A letter to a grieving brother-in-law in the loss of his wife )
I have been wanting to write to you ever since Dawn passed away to let you know what I believe about God and Heaven. I have a hard time explaining things in person so sometimes it’s easier to put my thoughts on paper.
I know that people have come up with new kinds through the years but they originated from the seed that was first put here by God. Think about the trees and the different stages they go through.
The acorn is gone and in it’s place there’s a whole new tree. When we die, our bodies are put in the ground too but God will give us our new bodies, which be much greater than our old ones as the oak tree is greater than the acorn.
I love Matthew 6:25&26. God tells us just as the birds of the air are taken care of by Him, we should not worry because He will also take care of us.
Won’t that be wonderful! I have peace in my heart of the prospect of dying because I know He will raise me up again with new everlasting life.
I could go on and on with different things about nature and how it relates in a spiritual way.
