What is the Meaning of Life?
Cruden’s Concordance defines life as “animated existence as distinguished from dead matter.”We all know when something is alive by the evidence exhibited. We know that a person or animal ceases to be alive when it stops breathing, communicating and functioning.
There is no life except from God. Even in our vast, yet limited, knowledge we cannot understand how God could do this, and maybe we never will, but it is even harder to believe that our complex and perfect creation was just the result of a series of freak accidents.
Why did God create human life?
Amen.”We are created for Him, for His pleasure.
