Do you want create your own cooking blog and you don't know how?
Choosing a good domain for your blog is key
Choose a name that is easy to remember, that means something. For example, if your name is Sara it could be something like lasrecetasdesara.com or similar.
It lor more explicit as possible. If your blog is about cooking recipes, then the domain name has to make it clear to whoever reads it that it is a recipe blog.
Use the extension .com, since it is the most used internationally. Only in the case of making a website only for Spain could you opt for extensions .es but never use rare extensions or extensions from other countries.
And that's it. Now what you already have the domain bought we are going to see the next step: the hosting.
Like to buy a domain, we are going to explain step by step how to buy a good hosting.
Select the hosting plan that best suits your needs. Here our recommendation is buy the plan for € 6,95 per month for being very powerful at a very reasonable price.
In point 5 you have to indicate that you want to install WordPress (it is recommended to always install the latest version) and as a final step you just have to click on the button Process the order. From here you just have to complete the registration as a new customer and that's it.
Raiola has a tool installed by default that allows you to install WordPress with 4 very easy clicks. If you want to see how you can do it, here is a video that explains the whole process step by step.
Now you only need get a design that you like and everything will be finished. When looking for design we have two options:
Use a payment design: This would be the most recommended option since for little more than 40 dollars we can have some really professional designs for our blog. Next I am going to show you some.
It is a very professional design and perfectly optimized for recipe blogs. You can download it for $ 48 click here.
Here we are going to give you a few tricks to achieve success with your new website.
Put one photograph of the finished dish at the beginning of the recipe. Then if you want you can put interior photos with the intermediate steps to follow, but the first photo that the reader always sees has to be of the finished recipe.
Your readers are your friends, talk to them as if they were lifelong friends with a close and warm tone. They will surely appreciate it!
Now we can only wish you good luck with your new blog and may you achieve many successes.
